Package: linop
Title: Matrix-Free Linear Operators with Evidence-Bearing Capabilities
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Gilles", "Colling", email = "gilles.colling051@gmail.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3070-6066"))
Description: Linear operators defined by their action rather than their entries.
    A 'linop' behaves like a matrix under ordinary arithmetic, composes lazily into
    a typed expression graph, and carries capabilities such as being Hermitian or
    positive definite together with a structured record of the argument that
    established them. A conformance suite lets an adapter author check that a new
    operator satisfies the contract.
